// A chain of 32 levels of blanket `extend … implements` blocks, each bounded by both
// interfaces of the next level (`extend<T extends A{k+1} & B{k+1}> T implements A{k}`). Each
// lookup checks both bounds, so without remembering finished lookups the work doubles per
// level; with it, each `(type, interface)` is looked up once, in sema and in lowering.

